    "created_at": "2018-02-28T16:33:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-28T16:34:19Z",
    "body": "The problem especially affects applications where one user might have access to a WebSocket endpoint while another doesn’t. I can reject the unauthorized user with HTTP 403, but there’s no way for the browser to tell the user that that’s the problem.\r\n\r\nI can at least distinguish an actual WebSocket error from a handshake failure by checking for whether an `open` event fired, but even then, I don’t know whether it was a 5xx error or what.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
