    "created_at": "2022-02-25T07:07:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-25T07:07:29Z",
    "body": "The fact that different types of errors are indistinguishable from JavaScript is an intentional feature of the WebSocket API to prevent it from being used for port scans and other attacks.\r\n\r\nIf at some point we implement CORS for WebSockets then that might change (but then you'd have to deal with CORS errors instead, so your life definitely wouldn't get easier).",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
